'''Herbert Hill''' (born October 1, 1984) is an American [[college basketball]] player that recently ended his career at [[Providence College]].  He stands 6'10" and weighs in at 240 pounds.  Coming seemingly out of nowhere after 3 very sub-par seasons for the [[Providence College Friars]], Herb, as he's called, propelled himself into a prospect for the [[NBA]] drafted, either late 1st round or early 2nd round.  This was due to the fact that he averaged 18.1 ppg and 8.8 rpg [http://www.sportsline.com/collegebasketball/players/playerpage/437954] his senior year, and is currently ranked as the 7th overall college basketball prospect by www.cbs.sportsline.com. In 2007, Herb became only the third Friar to lead the Big East Conference in scoring.  Eric Murdock 91' and Ryan Gomes 05' are the other two.

